[h1]TLB Keys[/h1]

Vehicle keys that your players manage in the field. Lock a vehicle for [b]your whole side[/b], for [b]your squad[/b], or to [b]one key[/b] in your pocket, all from the ACE interaction menu.

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/items.png[/img]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]CBA_A3[/b] and [b]ACE3[/b], built against 3.21.2
[*]Arma 3 v2.14 or newer
[*][b]TLB Interactions[/b], optional: vehicle locks are picked on its hands-on board
[*][b]TSP Breach[/b], optional: its lock pick kit works too
[/list]

[h2]Why[/h2]
ACE's vehicle keys open every vehicle of a side, and there is no good way to hand one out once a mission is running. A key is either in everyone's loadout or in nobody's.

TLB Keys replaces that with keys as real items. A vehicle nobody has locked is open, and the first player to lock one decides who else gets in.

[h2]The three ways to lock a vehicle[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Every key of the side[/b] - anyone with a blank key of that side. The shared motor pool.
[*][b]The owner's squad[/b] - the owner's squad, with a blank key of the side. A squad's own truck.
[*][b]Paired keys only[/b] - only keys cut to that vehicle. A command car nobody borrows.
[/list]

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/lock-vehicle-menu.png[/img]

Your unit chooses which of the three are allowed: force one way of working, or leave all three on and let whoever locks a vehicle decide.

[h2]What it adds[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Spare keys[/b]. Cut a blank key to a vehicle and hand it to someone.
[*][b]Change locks[/b]. Every key cut for the vehicle stops fitting, spares included.
[*][b]Master keys[/b], one per side, for Zeus, command and the motor pool. Can be hidden from the Arsenal.
[*][b]Key fobs[/b]. Program one and lock the vehicle from across the parking area, with a chirp.
[*][b]Key bindings[/b]. Lock the nearest vehicle your keys open without a menu, plus three key slots.
[*][b]Ignition lock[/b]. No key, no engine, even in the driver's seat.
[*][b]Locked cargo[/b] and an [b]inside handle[/b], like a real car door.
[*][b]Hand over key[/b], and [b]inspect[/b] or [b]label[/b] any key you carry.
[*][b]Lockpicking[/b] and [b]hotwiring[/b] for vehicles you have no key for.
[*][b]Vehicle types[/b]. Choose which kinds use keys at all: cars, APCs, tanks, helicopters, planes, boats.
[/list]

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/manage-keys-menu.png[/img]

The owner, and anyone with a master key, gets a Manage keys menu on the vehicle: who it opens for, cutting spares, programming fobs, changing the locks, naming it, handing it over, or giving it up.

[h2]Keys are items, and they stay items[/h2]
[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/arsenal-keys.png[/img]

A key carries its cut in the item itself, so it survives being dropped, stored in a crate, handed over, saved in an Arsenal loadout and respawning. Take an enemy's key off a body and it opens their vehicles: keys belong to a side, not to a player.

[h2]Lockpicking and hotwiring[/h2]
[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/lockpick-menu.png[/img]

A locked vehicle whose keys you do not have can be picked: a progress bar on its own, or [b]TLB Interactions[/b]' lockpicking board when that mod is loaded. The kit follows the mods you run - TLB Interactions', TSP Breach's, or the one TLB Keys ships - and the spare kit is hidden so nobody carries two.

Already inside a vehicle you have no key for? Hotwire it from the driver's seat. Picked and hotwired vehicles start without a key until someone with a key locks them again.

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/hotwire-menu.png[/img]

[h2]Your keys[/h2]
Everything you carry is in one menu on yourself: inspect a key to see which vehicles it opens right now, label it, wipe it blank, put it in a key slot for a key binding, or use a programmed fob.

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/own-keys-menu.png[/img]

[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/program-fob-menu.png[/img]

[h2]For mission makers[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Key Set module[/b]. Sync vehicles, crates and units: the vehicles are locked to the set, the crates hold its keys, the units spawn carrying one.
[*][b]Master Key module[/b]. Synced units start with a master key for their side.
[*][b]Eden attributes[/b] on every vehicle, and [b]Zeus modules[/b] to lock, strip keys, drop a key or hand out a master key.
[*][b]Scripting[/b]. Public functions to assign keys, hand them out and check access.
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys@main/docs/images/addon-options-general.png[/img]

Around 45 settings under [b]TLB Keys[/b] in the CBA settings menu, all server-forced: which lock modes are allowed, who may lock a vehicle first, who may manage one, spare keys, master keys, fobs, lockpicking, hotwiring, key bindings, and which vehicle types use keys.

[h2]Dedicated servers[/h2]
The mod is signed. Copy [b]TLBKeys01.bikey[/b] into your server's [i]keys[/i] folder, and load it on the server and every client.

[h2]Documentation[/h2]
Full documentation is on the GitHub wiki: a quick start, the player guide, key fobs and key bindings, mission making, every setting, troubleshooting and the changelog.

[url=https://github.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/wiki]github.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/wiki[/url]

